# Fixed 2026-10-02, defect 135's class, lane literals (the certain-fix
# audit's L2, and the shapes beside it). THIS FILE ENDS ITS LINES WITH CRLF,
# and `.gitattributes` keeps them (`-text`). Symptom: a string or a
# character literal left open at a CRLF line end cost `raw_carriage_return`,
# whose certain `\r` wrote the line end's carriage return into the literal,
# which stayed open; a backslash before the line end cost `unknown_escape`
# with a certain `\\` that did the same, and in a character literal a second
# message for one mistake. Cause: the scanners stopped at the line feed and
# read the carriage return before it as the literal's content. Now a
# carriage return that begins a CRLF line end ends the line, inside a
# literal or not: the literal is told unterminated, once, with no fix, and
# `--apply` leaves the case as it is (`literals.hero`). A carriage return
# anywhere else in a literal keeps its certain `\r`. Not yet among them: an
# `f"…"` literal left open at the line end with no backslash before it,
# whose scanner is `lex_interp.hero`'s `scan_piece`.

function a_string()
    print("abc)  #~ unterminated_string

function a_character()
    c = 'a  #~ unterminated_char
    print(c)

function a_closed_string_below()
    s = "abc  #~ unterminated_string
    t = "def"
    print(t)

function a_backslash_before_the_line_end()
    #~v unterminated_string
    s = "abc\
    print(1)

function a_backslash_in_a_character()
    #~v unterminated_char
    c = '\
    print(1)

function an_f_literal_before_its_first_hole()
    #~v unterminated_string
    s = f"abc\
    print(1)

function the_last_line()
    print("abc)  #~ unterminated_string
